I recorded the input variants and the sampling plan as four decisions (D3–D6) and moved H1388 from HYPOTHESES to PLAN_REVIEW. The plan brief, slide deck and checkpoint are next step's work.

**Decisions:**
- **D3, MSA:** chain B, 14-3-3 gamma, uses its ColabFold MSA of 10,377 sequences. Chain A, the 11-residue LARP1 peptide, runs on its sequence alone, with no paired MSA, because a peptide that short has no homologs worth aligning or pairing. I rejected deepening its MSA for the same reason.
- **D4, templates:** chain B gets its search templates plus 6S9K chain A pinned first. That's a 1.60 Å structure of 14-3-3 gamma with a phosphopeptide in the groove, and it has to be passed in by hand because AF3 drops near-identical templates. I chose not to give a two-chain template: there is no public 14-3-3:LARP1 structure, and copying the bound caspase-2 peptide would force its residue positions onto a different sequence. 6ZBT and 6A5S are the fallbacks.
- **D5, phosphoserine:** pSer7 (LARP1 Ser548) goes into chain A as a modification, next to an unmodified control run. The engine's input builder has no option for a modification, so it has to be written into the built input file afterwards. AF3 and Protenix both read that field. Boltz-2 and OF3 get it only if their converters pass it through; otherwise they run unmodified and are labelled as such. I rejected substituting glutamate at S7: it is a poor stand-in for the phosphate the binding pocket recognises.
- **D6, sampling:** all runs are one peptide on one 14-3-3 chain:

  | Predictor | Phosphoserine | Seeds × samples |
  |---|---|---|
  | AF3 (lead) | yes | 20 × 5 |
  | AF3 (control) | no | 10 × 5 |
  | Protenix | yes | 10 × 5 |
  | Boltz-2 | as converted | 10 × 5 |
  | OF3 | as converted | 10 × 5 |

  That is about 300 models. My estimate is about 5 GPU-hours, capped at 20 of the 400 h budget. At selection, a model must have the phosphate within 4 Å of B K49/R56/R131/Y132 to pass; confidence only ranks models within a predictor. More sampling only if the first results disagree on where or which way the peptide sits.

**Before inputs are built:** the note I left on the target asks for two checks. The modification has to be added to the AF3 and Protenix inputs. And I took the 14-3-3 chain in 6S9K to be chain A without opening the entry, so that needs confirming before it is pinned.

**Next step:** build the slide deck, write the plan brief and open the plan checkpoint, which I answer myself under the mandate.

